<title>MEXICO: Tribasa signs $100 mln road finance deal.</title>
<headline>Tribasa signs $100 mln road finance deal.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction firm Grupo Tribasa signed a $100 million deal to finance the construction of the Acceso Norte to Concepcion highway in Chile, a company executive told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal has just been signed in Santiago de Chile, and completes financing for the project, which is already 50 percent built,&quot; said deputy COO Fernando Gutierrez Ochoa in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>The Acceso Norte to Concepcion highway will be 62 miles long. Tribasa has an 80 percent stake and the remaining 20 percent is held by Chilean firm Nel Latour. The estimated cost of the project is $170 million.</p>
</text>
